 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nMAC token header generation broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `prepare_mac_header` function is no longer working correctly. When trying to generate MAC authentication headers, the function fails to produce the expected output.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.tokens import prepare_mac_header\n\n# Basic MAC header preparation\ntoken = 'access_token_value'\nuri = 'https://example.com/resource'\nkey = 'mac_key_value'\nhttp_method = 'GET'\n\n# This should work but doesn't produce expected results\nheader = prepare_mac_header(\n    token=token,\n    uri=uri, \n    key=key,\n    http_method=http_method,\n    hash_algorithm='hmac-sha-1'\n)\n```\n\nThe function appears to be missing critical components needed for proper MAC signature generation. MAC authentication requires specific hash algorithm handling and body hash computation that seems to have been removed.\n</issue>\n",
